    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class; the other two files are its base/support). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the salutation feature so `salutation = title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nChanges, each placed where that concern already lives:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (DTOs are generated from it):\n   - Added optional `title` input to the `OwnerFields` schema (values MR/MRS/MS/DR, `maxLength: 3`).\n   - Added read-only `salutation` to the `Owner` schema.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a persisted `title` field/column with getter/setter (and to `toString`), so it survives POST \u2192 GET.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added a `salutation(Owner)` helper plus its `@Mapping`, sitting alongside the other derived display fields (`displayName`, `initials`, \u2026). This is the single spot both the OfficeFloor and Spring MVC arms compute it, via `toOwnerDto`. `title` itself auto-maps by name through `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)`, covering the create path (`BuildOwner`).\n\n4. **`ApplyOwner`** \u2014 added `owner.setTitle(request.getTitle())` so the PUT/update path copies `title` alongside its sibling field assignments.\n\n5. **`schema.sql`** for all four dialects (hsqldb/h2/postgres/mysql) \u2014 added the `title` column, since the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none` with explicit schema scripts.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
